From dd16721566236a4f4ceb868129ce97af764be417 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Walker <ben@nvidia.com>
Date: Fri, 30 May 2025 10:42:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/21] sock/uring: Remove spdk_pipe support

This will hurt performance in some cases, so it cannot be merged without
the following patches in this series. However, it is a required change
to support zero copy rx.

Change-Id: Icb6b6a49490b749547b1ee7eeff9de2107c3d09c
Signed-off-by: Ben Walker <ben@nvidia.com>
---
 CHANGELOG.md              |   3 +
 deprecation.md            |   5 +
 include/spdk/sock.h       |   2 +-
 module/sock/uring/uring.c | 232 +++++---------------------------------
 python/spdk/cli/sock.py   |   2 +-
 schema/schema.yaml        |   2 +-
 6 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 205 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 050bf3896..ca3d0d810 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -272,6 +272,9 @@ removed in v26.09:
   `spdk_sock_group_provide_buf`, `spdk_sock_group_get_buf`) will be replaced by a new
   zero-copy API.
 
+The uring sock implementation no longer supports `enable_recv_pipe`; the option is accepted as
+a no-op for uring and only applies to posix/ssl.
+
 ### trace
 
 The shared-memory trace file (`spdk_trace_file`) was reorganized into a sequence of typed sections
diff --git a/deprecation.md b/deprecation.md
index dcde4ee2b..e1f28d947 100644
--- a/deprecation.md
+++ b/deprecation.md
@@ -112,6 +112,11 @@ per I/O on the DIF path (the old in-place transport-side path is gone).
 
 ### sock
 
+#### uring `enable_recv_pipe`
+
+`enable_recv_pipe` is no longer used by the uring sock implementation. The option remains
+accepted by `spdk_sock_impl_set_opts`, but it is a no-op for uring and only applies to posix/ssl.
+
 #### `nvmf_create_transport`
 
 buf-cache-size parameter is deprecated in favor of iobuf-small-cache-size and will be removed in 26.09 release.
